  "notes": "WLF482 is a passive, unterminated 2RU \"longframe\" (full-size 1/4\") TRS patch bay with 48 jacks arranged in two rows of 24 (front-panel positions 1-24 top, 25-48 bottom), per the manufacturer's official installation drawing (whirlwindusa.com Support/Downloads page for WLF482, hosted on their Webflow CDN). The drawing's reference schematic labels each jack circuit S/R/T with normal contacts RN/TN, confirming standard half-normalled 1/4\" TRS wiring - hence connector trs-6.35 for all 48 front jacks (modeled as bidirectional, as is standard for patch-bay jacks). Being \"unterminated,\" the rear of the unit ships with no connectors at all - solder lugs/wire-wrap posts for the installer's own cabling - so no standard connector id applies there and rear terminals are omitted from the ports list. No power input; this is a fully passive panel. The drawing itself is an ADC Telecommunications OEM drawing (catalog # P-KIT-3-WW) supplied by Whirlwind for this rebadged product, which is why confidence is medium rather than high - it confirms mechanical/jack layout precisely but is not a marketing spec sheet with a jack-type sentence spelled out in prose. Retailer listings (Full Compass, Adorama, ProAudioSolutions) corroborate: \"Patch bay - longframe, 2 x 24, unterminated, 2 RU.\"",
